<title>USA: Global Industrial Q1 Jan 31 net loss.</title>
<headline>Global Industrial Q1 Jan 31 net loss.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>GLOBAL INDUSTRIAL TECHNOLOGIES, INC. AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>		 Consolidated Condensed Statements of Earnings</p>
<p>			(In millions except per share data)</p>
<p>							 Three months ended</p>
<p>							  January 31,</p>
<p>						     1997	 1996</p>
<p>							 (Unaudited)</p>
<p> Total Revenues				 132.3	149.9</p>
<p> Net earnings				  (11.4)	  5.6</p>
<p> Earnings per common share		 (O.50)	 0.25</p>
<p> Average common shares outstanding	 22.7	 22.6</p>
<p>NOTE: Results include a $20.5 million pre-tax charge to earnings related to the divestiture of three of its operating units.</p>
<p>Excluding the effect of the charge-off or any contribution from those three operating units, Global reported earnings of $0.18 per share on revenues of $132.3 million and operating profits of $12.0 million.  For the same period a year ago, Global reported earnings of $0.25 per share on revenues of $149.9 million and operating profits of $12.9 million.</p>
</text>
